240,269,273,349,353,356,367,374,379,401,434,437],[229,230,25],"h2",{"id":231},"overview",[233,234,235],"p",{},"Kinotic OS is a full-stack application platform that handles service communication, persistence, authentication, authorization, deployment, and observability. The system is composed of several core components that work together to provide a seamless development and runtime experience.",[229,237,239],{"id":238},"core-components","Core Components",[241,242,243,251,257,263],"ul",{},[244,245,246,250],"li",{},[247,248,249],"strong",{},"Kinotic Server"," — The central platform server built on Spring Boot. Manages service registration, authentication, session management, and coordinates all platform operations.",[244,252,253,256],{},[247,254,255],{},"RPC Gateway"," — Routes remote procedure calls between clients and published services over STOMP\u002FWebSocket.",[244,258,259,262],{},[247,260,261],{},"Persistence Layer"," — Provides automatic CRUD operations for entities backed by Elasticsearch.",[244,264,265,268],{},[247,266,267],{},"Auth System"," — Handles authentication (email\u002Fpassword and OIDC). Supports three authorization hierarchies: System, Organization, and Application.",[229,270,272],{"id":271},"tech-stack","Tech Stack",[274,275,276,289],"table",{},[277,278,279],"thead",{},[280,281,282,286],"tr",{},[283,284,285],"th",{},"Component",[283,287,288],{},"Technology",[290,291,292,301,309,317,325,333,341],"tbody",{},[280,293,294,298],{},[295,296,297],"td",{},"Orchestration",[295,299,300],{},"Kubernetes",[280,302,303,306],{},[295,304,305],{},"Build Isolation",[295,307,308],{},"Firecracker VMs",[280,310,311,314],{},[295,312,313],{},"Runtime",[295,315,316],{},"Bun",[280,318,319,322],{},[295,320,321],{},"Database",[295,323,324],{},"Postgres (Hibernate Reactive)",[280,326,327,330],{},[295,328,329],{},"Search\u002FPersistence",[295,331,332],{},"Elasticsearch",[280,334,335,338],{},[295,336,337],{},"Logging",[295,339,340],{},"Grafana Loki",[280,342,343,346],{},[295,344,345],{},"Payments",[295,347,348],{},"Stripe Connect",[229,350,352],{"id":351},"communication","Communication",[233,354,355],{},"Services communicate via STOMP over WebSocket, with messages routed by CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier). Each service, method, and event stream is addressable through a CRI, which follows the format:",[357,358,363],"pre",{"className":359,"code":361,"language":362},[360],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[364,365,361],"code",{"__ignoreMap":366},"",[233,368,369,370,373],{},"The RPC gateway uses CRIs to route requests to the correct service instance, apply versioning, and enforce scope-based multi-tenancy. See the ",[371,372,205],"a",{"href":206}," reference for details.",[375,376,378],"h3",{"id":377},"never-block-the-event-loop","Never block the event loop",[233,380,381,382,385,386,389,390,389,393,396,397,400],{},"A Java service published with ",[364,383,384],{},"@Publish"," is invoked on a Vert.x event loop it shares with the other services on the node, the same rule Vert.x sets for its own handlers. A method returns a ",[364,387,388],{},"Future",", ",[364,391,392],{},"CompletableFuture",[364,394,395],{},"Mono"," or ",[364,398,399],{},"Flux"," and lets the work complete off the loop; a method that is slow, because it blocks on a synchronous client, a lock or a sleep, or because it does heavy CPU work, hands that work off inside itself:",[357,402,406],{"className":403,"code":404,"language":405,"meta":366,"style":366},"language-java shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","@Override\npublic Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n}\n","java",[364,407,408,416,422,428],{"__ignoreMap":366},[409,410,413],"span",{"class":411,"line":412},"line",1,[409,414,415],{},"@Override\n",[409,417,419],{"class":411,"line":418},2,[409,420,421],{},"public Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n",[409,423,425],{"class":411,"line":424},3,[409,426,427],{},"    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n",[409,429,431],{"class":411,"line":430},4,[409,432,433],{},"}\n",[233,435,436],{},"The platform never hands off on a service's behalf. A method that blocks stalls every service sharing its loop, and Vert.x's blocked-thread checker reports it in the log.",[438,439,440],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":366,"searchDepth":418,"depth":418,"links":442},[443,444,445,446],{"id":231,"depth":418,"text":25},{"id":238,"depth":418,"text":239},{"id":271,"depth":418,"text":272},{"id":351,"depth":418,"text":352,"children":447},[448],{"id":377,"depth":424,"text":378},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.","md",null,{},{"icon":151},{"title":148,"description":449},"LVvYv_3MQRd0KP7EuURGbqzxnublPPEXhVfaIKf_Pf4",[457,459],{"title":139,"path":140,"stem":141,"description":458,"icon":60,"children":-1},"Complete SQL grammar reference for migration scripts.",{"title":153,"path":154,"stem":155,"description":460,"icon":6,"children":-1},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.",1789529834367]